# Spider-Verse: "Do this only once each turn", and "Any instances of the ability already on the stack when you choose to copy a spell will
# have no effect" (the ruling). Wrenn's Resolve exiles two Lightning Bolts; on turn five the first is cast at Bot2 and, holding priority,
# the second at Bot2's Ornithopter, so both triggers are on the stack. The later one resolves first: it is asked, and the copy "may choose
# new targets" - Bot2 in place of the Ornithopter. The earlier trigger then asks nothing. The Bolt at the Ornithopter kills it, so Bot2 takes
# the first Bolt and the copy, six in all, and the Ornithopter is dead. The copy of an instant gains no haste (it is no permanent).

